Game Setup &
Standard Turn
<BOLD>1.</BOLD> First choose somebody to Host the game. This should be a player that is familiar with the game. It is the job of the Host to run the game. The Host may take the Host card to show their status as the Host.
<BOLD>2.</BOLD> The Host should then select as many cards as there are players. For unexperienced players, check Card Mix on more details on how to pick cards. They will then deal one card to each player, face-down. The players then look at their card, but may not share them with other players.
<BOLD>3.</BOLD> The Host then puts the town to sleep and the first night begins. Depending on the cards in play, the Host now wakes up certain roles. For more details, check the action order at the end of the booklet.
<BOLD>4.</BOLD> After all roles have used their abilities, the Host wakes the town up and reveals who has died. The players that have died now reveal their card (when playing with flips) and are no longer allowed to use their abilities, discuss or participate in the game.
<BOLD>5.</BOLD> The players now have a chance to debate.
<BOLD>6.</BOLD> When enough time has passed, the Host will end the discussion and starts the vote. Now, all players will need to point at another player they want to eliminate at the same time. The player with the most votes is eliminated. If there is a tie, nobody is eliminated.
<BOLD>7.</BOLD> The players now fall asleep again, and the night begins again.
